{
  "name": "get_processing_run",
  "title": "Get processing run",
  "description": "Read one bounded durable minutes-ensemble run using meeting_id, authorized scope and opaque run_id. Include partial successful work without treating it as published. The snapshot carries planned selections/policy and canonical generator slots; executed nodes keep separate historical origin and nullable confirmed-retry lineage. A successful retry may use a different connection without rewriting its original unknown ancestry. Volatile jobs and durable runs are distinct; no legacy single-generation or ASR run is fabricated. Without an active execution-lease owner, recover stale running as interrupted when no unresolved pending call remains, or blocked with unknown details otherwise. Restore valid receipts without resending and never infer completion from a missing job. Local read only; no filesystem path input. On failure return error_envelope (isError=true) with code not_found, scope_denied, invalid_argument or internal.",
  "annotations": {
    "readOnlyHint": true,
    "destructiveHint": false,
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false
  },
